# ticking-clock — pattern
@id ticking-clock  @kind pattern  @layer library  @author toine  @lang en

## summary
~ A visible resource runs down with session time. It gives the session a length, makes every request cost something, and offers an ending of its own when it runs out.

## roles
role clock : clock : the resource that runs down (declared in pack.json clocks)
role keeper : character : who notices and says it
role half_line : line : said once at half
role low_line : line : said once at the low threshold
role critical_line : line : said once at the critical threshold
role warning_cue : cue : the sound the resource makes when it is low
role run_out : ending : the ending family when it runs out

## params
param half = 0.5 : fraction for the first notice
param low = 0.25 : fraction for the low notice
param critical = 0.10 : fraction where the keeper talks less
param degrade = 0.35 : image degradation at critical

## principles
! $keeper mentions $clock at most once per threshold, never as a countdown.
~0.6 The closer to the end, the fewer words.

## rules
when clock.below($clock, $half) once -> say($half_line) {half}
when clock.below($clock, $low) once -> say($low_line), sound($warning_cue), image.degrade(0.15) {low}
when clock.below($clock, $critical) once -> say($critical_line), image.degrade($degrade), speech.shorten(0.5) {critical}
when clock.below($clock, 0) once if not ending.any -> ending($run_out) {run-out}

## beats_hint
hint the clock is seen before it is mentioned
hint the last beat should be reachable at the low threshold, not after

## variations
variation generous : half = 0.4, low = 0.15, critical = 0.05; the clock is atmosphere more than pressure
variation hidden : the keeper never mentions it; only the image and the cue tell
